{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ImQChiralityIsBarInvolution","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ImQChiralityIsBarInvolution","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ImQRealityLocus"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.chirality_invariance_forces_real_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.chirality_invariance_forces_real_q","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQChiralityIsBarInvolution.lean#L135-L156","doc":"**Second leg — granting candidate (i)'s identification collapses it.**\nHypotheses, each doing visible work:\n\n* `hschwarz` — Schwarz reflection, `Q_β(q̄) = conj(Q_β(q))`: an arithmetic fact\n  about a real-coefficient rational function times a modulus (probe residual\n  `0.0` at 50 dps over three points × two extensions). In components, the\n  imaginary part **negates**.\n* `hchiral` — **the physics premise**, and the only one: `Q_β` is\n  chirality-invariant, so `Q_β(q̄) = Q_β(q)` and the imaginary part is\n  **unchanged**. A Q-value is a parity-even energy. It is a hypothesis\n  precisely so that it is never assumed inside a proof.\n* `hform` — E2's exact imaginary-part numerator from `ImQRealityLocus`.\n\nThe first two say the same quantity both negates and does not, so it vanishes;\n`im_qbeta_zero_iff_e2` turns that into `Im q = 0` on the substrate branch. Note\nthe two premises pull in opposite directions and that is the entire content:\nneither alone gives anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bar_involution_of_substrate_is_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bar_involution_of_substrate_is_real","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQChiralityIsBarInvolution.lean#L124-L133","doc":"**The corpus's mirror of the substrate is real.** `q ↦ q⁻¹` sends a real\n`q > 1` to a real number in `(0, 1)` — so the chirality flip the corpus uses\nneeds no imaginary part whatsoever, which is the positive form of the first\nleg. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.substrate_off_unit_circle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.substrate_off_unit_circle","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQChiralityIsBarInvolution.lean#L113-L122","doc":"**The substrate is off the unit circle.** `q₀` is real with `1 < q₀`, so\n`|q₀|² = q₀² > 1`. Hence `conj_eq_inv_iff_modulus_one` does not apply there and\nthe two chirality candidates are genuinely different maps — measured `0.20906`\napart, 18.83 % of `q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.conj_eq_inv_iff_modulus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.conj_eq_inv_iff_modulus_one","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ImQChiralityIsBarInvolution.lean#L90-L111","doc":"**`q̄ = q⁻¹` exactly on the unit circle.** In real coordinates `q = x + iy`,\n`q⁻¹ = (x − iy)/s` with `s = x² + y²`, so `q̄ − q⁻¹ = (x − iy)(1 − 1/s)` and both\ncomponents carry the same factor `s − 1`. For `q ≠ 0` the two operations agree\niff `s = 1`.\n\nThis is the whole first leg: candidate (i)'s identification of chirality with\nconjugation is the corpus's identification of it with the bar involution\n**precisely on `|q| = 1`**, which is the regime candidate (i) names, and it is\nnot the regime the substrate is in. ","signatureChunk":0}]}